# Harnesses you save yourself no longer land here — they go to
#
#     %LOCALAPPDATA%\Physalia\PRESETS\User\        (Windows)
#     ~/.local/share/Physalia/PRESETS/User/        (elsewhere)
#
# because Rhino replaces a plug-in's install directory wholesale when it updates the package, and it
# does that silently at startup. A harness you saved would have gone with it. Anything already in
# here is carried across the first time the new build runs.
#
# The presets in the "Physalia" folder beside this one are still read from the package: they are ours
# rather than yours, and they are meant to be replaced by an update.
#
# Use "Save Harness as Preset…" — on a Harness component's right-click menu, or on the "Harness"
# widget at the top-left of the canvas while you are inside one. Anything saved shows up in the chat
# window's "Add preset" gallery under "User". You can also drop a .gh or .phy into that folder by
# hand: a preset is an ordinary Grasshopper file holding one harness's worth of pipeline, and it must
# contain a Chat component or it cannot be loaded back.
#
# This file only exists to keep the folder in git.
